From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:40:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_qca: give a cold WCN3950 time to boot after
 the power-on pulse

qca_send_power_pulse() sleeps 100 ms after the power-on pulse, and
qca_setup() then reopens the port and reads the version. A WCN3950
powered from cold rails needs ~130 ms on the MANGMI Air X before it
listens (its CTS pulses when it is up), so that first command is lost:
every boot waited out the 2 s command timeout and only came up on the
retry, where the chip, powered once already, is up in ~45 ms.

Wait 200 ms after a WCN3950's power-on pulse; the other WCN399x keep
100 ms.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -1461,9 +1461,11 @@ static int qca_send_power_pulse(struct hci_uart *hu, bool on)
 	serdev_device_wait_until_sent(hu->serdev, timeout);
 	hci_uart_set_flow_control(hu, false);

-	/* Give to controller time to boot/shutdown */
+	/* Give to controller time to boot/shutdown. A WCN3950 booting from
+	 * cold rails takes ~130 ms, and a command sent before then is lost.
+	 */
 	if (on)
-		msleep(100);
+		msleep(qca_soc_type(hu) == QCA_WCN3950 ? 200 : 100);
 	else
 		usleep_range(1000, 10000);

